From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:39:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] twinapi: add VirtualDesktopManager.

Word asks twinapi's VirtualDesktopManager whether its windows are on the
virtual desktop the user is looking at, and the class was not there.

As Windows 11 answers it (tools/vdmprobe in the wine-altars tree), for the
one desktop there is here:

- IsWindowOnCurrentVirtualDesktop is TRUE for any handle, a hidden window,
  a child, the desktop window or one that is no window, and for NULL too,
  though then with E_INVALIDARG.
- GetWindowDesktopId has the desktop's id for the shown top level windows
  of applications, and TYPE_E_ELEMENTNOTFOUND with GUID_NULL for every other
  handle; E_INVALIDARG for NULL.  The id is kept where explorer keeps it,
  under Explorer\VirtualDesktops, and made the first time it is needed.
- MoveWindowToDesktop takes a window of one's own, shown, hidden or a child,
  to that desktop, and to no other: TYPE_E_ELEMENTNOTFOUND; another
  process's window is E_ACCESSDENIED, and NULL E_INVALIDARG.
- The object is agile.

IVirtualDesktopManager and the class are added to shobjidl.idl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 79ed6181b854176e95b0fbfce21accb85a08dad5)

